user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2022, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T08:31:55-07:00","id":1483131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1482923#post1482923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point is there anyone who still believes that its actually going to come out? I mean if there is I have some riverside infrastructure that I'm looking to offload. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They will release it, if only to try to get back some of the developement costs, it will most likely suck but some might still buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T08:33:47-07:00","id":1483132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1483130#post1483130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a decent article on the subject: <a href=\"https://www.looper.com/353416/game-actors-who-are-gorgeous-in-real-life/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.looper.com/353416/game-a...-in-real-life/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe I'm missing something but what does an article about voice actors got to do with bloodlines 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T08:46:06-07:00","id":1483133,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Bloodlines 2, I have very little confidence at this point. The longer a project is delayed, the less likely whatever comes out will actually be good. Especially if it's divorced from the artists that drove its creative process.<br /> <br /> Other writers can be brought on. But they would be trying to bolt together an existing game into something coherent. This can work well. I'm reminded of Demon's Souls, a game that no one at FromSoft thought had a chance, but which Hidetake Miyazaki came in and transformed into a cult classic that turned into a beloved franchise. (Miyazaki himself is now FromSoft's president.)<br /> <br /> But just because it CAN work out well, doesn't mean it WILL. Again, the longer it goes on, the less confidence it inspires.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to stress that, the longer a project takes to deliver, the less likely it will be to live up to the elevated expectations of customers waiting for it. Even if, say, Duke Nukem Forever hadn't been a steaming turd on release, and instead was a good game, it would never have lived up to the decade plus wait to see it produced. (Which makes it all the more sad that, around a decade earlier, Duke Nukem Forever HAD an almost complete build, that got recently leaked. The developers just didn't want to release it unless it was the most cutting edge.)<br /> <br /> If Bloodlines 2 releases, is it really going to be worth it? Could it EVER live up to the hype it generated? Especially now, after its fraught development?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> On another subject...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1482903#post1482903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warhammer 40k runs into the issue that the stuff that mainly gets discussed about, the stuff that sort of ends up being representative of the game, is Space Marines, Chaos Marines and Orks. Stuff like the Tau or Sisters of Silence or such are things you're going to have to delve into the wiki to learn about. So it ends up being a bit problematic when the poster children of 40k are either &quot;No Girls Allowed&quot; or male presenting. It gives a strong impression of the setting, even if it isn't entirely accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> People want female Space Marines because Space Marines are, for better or worse, the default Protagonist faction of 40K. A faction that gives players the maximum ability to customize their force, in paint scheme and theme and lore...<br /> <br /> ...EXCEPT when it comes to not letting any of them be women. Space Marines can be anything, <i>except women</i>. No girls allowed.<br /> <br /> Obviously there is female representation in other factions. But those are generally more narrow in thematic and aesthetic scope (not to mention gameplay), and aren't as front and center as Space Marines. Eldar, regardless of version, aren't as prominent or popular or supported as Space Marines. At least in Age of Sigmar, the Stormcast Eternals have less of an omnipresence, so other factions, like the Daughters of Khaine, can get more of a spotlight. (Also, Stormcast Eternals not only get to be women, but get female-coded sculpts. I personally don't think that's as necessary with Space Marines - just giving them female-coded head options would be enough - but at least AoS gives the &quot;Ground Marines&quot; the option.)<br /> <br /> And then we have the all-female factions of 40K, like Sisters of Battle and Sisters of Silence. First, they are, again, not as prominent as Space Marines. They are single factions, compared to Space Marines that are basically half the factions in the game. (Assuming you count all the specialist chapters and Chaos Space Marines). Sisters of Silence aren't even a whole faction, they're second fiddle to the Custodes, which are Space Marines in everything but name.<br /> <br /> Sisters of Battle, meanwhile, have only one thematic mode: Nuns with Guns. They do this beautifully, but that's the box they're limited to. If you don't like Nuns with Guns, SoB have nothing to offer you.<br /> <br /> That's why it's important for there to be women Space Marines. Not only being put front and center in the game, but giving that option within factions that give maximum creative and aesthetic and thematic freedom.<br /> <br /> Women players should be allowed to see themselves in the default protagonists of 40K. And have the ability to choose for themselves what that means.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:40:21-07:00","id":1483140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1483131#post1483131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They will release it, if only to try to get back some of the developement costs, it will most likely suck but some might still buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's usually a bad move if that's the case. In such situations releasing whatever you have is better than keep developing it, as it is just accruing more costs.<br /> <br /> No, they probably still think it can be a success or, at least, worth their investment somehow. They want it to be a success and so keep throwing money and time at it.<br /> <br /> Maybe it will pay off. Sometimes weird things come out of Development Hell, and just a handful of them are good, so I won't keep low expectations as much as no expectation at all. I don't think guessing at this point is worth anything, except maybe help to keep the project afloat, which isn't necessarily good. I'll just wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:46:23-07:00","id":1483143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1483132#post1483132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe I'm missing something but what does an article about voice actors got to do with bloodlines 2?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.looper.com/868097/whatever-happened-to-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.looper.com/868097/whatev...-bloodlines-2/</a><br /> <br /> Not a thing.<br /> <br /> It's called cutting and pasting a link and for whatever reason, the cutting not happening so the previous cut thing was still there.<br /> <br /> My bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1483133#post1483133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of Bloodlines 2, I have very little confidence at this point. The longer a project is delayed, the less likely whatever comes out will actually be good. Especially if it's divorced from the artists that drove its creative process.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Witcher 3, notably, adverts this completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:46:50-07:00","id":1483145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1483140#post1483140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's usually a bad move if that's the case. In such situations releasing whatever you have is better than keep developing it, as it is just accruing more costs.<br /> <br /> No, they probably still think it can be a success or, at least, worth their investment somehow. They want it to be a success and so keep throwing money and time at it.<br /> <br /> Maybe it will pay off. Sometimes weird things come out of Development Hell, and just a handful of them are good, so I won't keep low expectations as much as no expectation at all. I don't think guessing at this point is worth anything, except maybe help to keep the project afloat, which isn't necessarily good. I'll just wait and see.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe what they have is not in a playable state, we literally know nothing about it so it could be anything.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't trust execs to actually know anything about what the public might like, cyberpunk 2077 is a great example of it, if the game flops then it will not be their fault anyway so of course they are going to release it anyway.<br /> <br /> With this I'm not saying that I actively hope it will fail, if they will manage to make a good game then all the better but frankly, given the results with basically all of the new licensed WoD games so far, I really don't have high expectations...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T09:48:10-07:00","id":1483147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1483143#post1483143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.looper.com/868097/whatever-happened-to-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.looper.com/868097/whatev...-bloodlines-2/</a><br /> <br /> Not a thing.<br /> <br /> It's called cutting and pasting a link and for whatever reason, the cutting not happening so the previous cut thing was still there.<br /> <br /> My bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Witcher 3, notably, adverts this completely.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I actually missed this article.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T10:32:24-07:00","id":1483154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1483145#post1483145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe what they have is not in a playable state, we literally know nothing about it so it could be anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is not in a playable state, then you scrap the project altogether. My point was about you reaching a practical dead end.<br /> <br /> Executives don't have to know how to please the public or how to make a game, they must know how to run a business and keep things from becoming sinkholes of money. Rushed games certainly show it when they're finally released, but my point is that development is a cost, and a hefty one.<br /> <br /> So, in the specific scenario of them wanting to just get back development costs, making <i>more</i> development costs is a bad strategy. And I was talking specifically about this.<br /> <br /> They either are making a stupid move <i>or</i> they still believe in the project (or in another project altogether under the same name, as we don't know shit about the new developer). Believing in the project is another set of scenarios entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T10:47:09-07:00","id":1483156,"title":"","content":"This 40k discussion is really one of the big bleeding hearts of the issue with V5<br /> <br /> 40k, like the World of Darkness, is a satire, a dark joke, where the dysfunctional theocratic fascists who treat lives like dirt are The Good Guys. Space marines have a spare of every extra organ except for their brain because denying them some extra intelligence is <i>funny</i>. Making the warrior-monk super soldiers gender inclusive is antithetical to the <i>satire </i>the series is trying to convey. <br /> <br /> Vampire's the much same, only there's a reversal: 40k takes a jab at the improbable nightmare scenario, Vampire has the nightmare scenario as parallel to reality: your boss is actually an evil bloodsucking parasite who controls the city from the shadows, and in the WoD he might just be a vampire. Vampire isn't supposed to be a setting that provides you with easily accessible social justice, it's supposed to hit you in the face with a lack of social justice. V5, meanwhile, betrays both the Satirical nature of the series and the semblance to reality by... making everyone equal and presenting scenarios that do not have parallels in the real world (IE where's my SI taking out the world's parasites? I see nothing) There's no umph behind the blows, no intent behind the strikes, and most of the punches miss. And things will continue to be divisive until things get back on track and we square VTM back into the easy territory of -our reality but the bad stuff is exaggerated-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T11:42:37-07:00","id":1483160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know, and don't much care. I see no reason to directly or indirectly give Paradox money.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Then why post at all?<br /> <br /> Specifically, this is a warning not to threadcrap.</b></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Actionable disinterest is a position whether you like it or not. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>No, it isn't.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T13:06:48-07:00","id":1483166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482735-what-do-you-predict-will-happen-when-vtm-bloodlines-2-is-finally-if-ever-released?p=1483156#post1483156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This 40k discussion is really one of the big bleeding hearts of the issue with V5<br /> <br /> 40k, like the World of Darkness, is a satire, a dark joke, where the dysfunctional theocratic fascists who treat lives like dirt are The Good Guys. Space marines have a spare of every extra organ except for their brain because denying them some extra intelligence is <i>funny</i>. Making the warrior-monk super soldiers gender inclusive is antithetical to the <i>satire </i>the series is trying to convey.<br /> <br /> Vampire's the much same, only there's a reversal: 40k takes a jab at the improbable nightmare scenario, Vampire has the nightmare scenario as parallel to reality: your boss is actually an evil bloodsucking parasite who controls the city from the shadows, and in the WoD he might just be a vampire. Vampire isn't supposed to be a setting that provides you with easily accessible social justice, it's supposed to hit you in the face with a lack of social justice. V5, meanwhile, betrays both the Satirical nature of the series and the semblance to reality by... making everyone equal and presenting scenarios that do not have parallels in the real world (IE where's my SI taking out the world's parasites? I see nothing) There's no umph behind the blows, no intent behind the strikes, and most of the punches miss. And things will continue to be divisive until things get back on track and we square VTM back into the easy territory of -our reality but the bad stuff is exaggerated-</div> </div> </div> </div>In broad terms I agree.<br /> <br /> Though I am not sure either is actually satire because for something to be satire it has to expose the stupidity or vices of the subject matter and then condemn them. In both 40K and V:tM you get to explore the nightmare scenarios, but there is no critique for saying &quot;I like it here&quot;. Granted 40K is one of the few settings where none of its fans would ever want to live there.<br /> <br /> What makes the &quot;punch in the face&quot; as you put it happen is the concept that the horrible nightmare options are functional strategies, or in some cases the only strategies. Social justice is essentially predicated on the idea that such strategies are indefensible and never work.<br /> <br /> So perhaps it could be said that the Satire aspect is actually aimed at the more social justice / morality brigade concepts, but if so I agree that from what I have seen of V5, it is doing a poor job of it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T13:10:54-07:00","id":1483167,"title":"","content":"I miss the days when conservatives had the courage of their convictions to just drop the N-bomb and whatnot. Nobody's fooled by the hiding behind &quot;woke&quot; and &quot;social justice.&quot; Everybody knows what you mean. Just say what you mean.<br /> <br /> Thanks for shitting up yet another thread with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T14:16:27-07:00","id":1483172,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Yeah, this thread did not abide by the request to avoid getting into criticizing &quot;woke&quot; politics and social justice.<br /> <br /> Closed.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> And &quot;woke&quot; is a word that is created for and by minorities in America to refer to awareness about social injustice. It has been co-opted by the Alt-Right.<br /> <br /> Using it as a pejorative is banned.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-05-2022, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}